{"node":{"id":"HP:0000239","label":"Large fontanelles","ic":4.02,"definition":"In newborns, the two frontal bones, two parietal bones, and one occipital bone are joined by fibrous sutures, which form a small posterior fontanelle, and a larger, diamond-shaped anterior fontanelle. These regions allow for the skull to pass the birth canal and for later growth. The fontanelles gradually ossify, whereby the posterior fontanelle usually closes by eight weeks and the anterior fontanelle by the 9th to 16th month of age. Large fontanelles are diagnosed if the fontanelles are larger than age-dependent norms."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0013952","label":"peroxisome biogenesis disorder 13A (Zellweger)","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_7fcfc6f8e30b","source":"MONDO:0013952","target":"HP:0000239","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:614887 · PMID:15146459","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15146459/","level":"observed","date":"2023-03-06","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Peroxisome biogenesis disorder 13A (Zellweger): Large fontanelles (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0008954","label":"peroxisome biogenesis disorder 2A (Zellweger)","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_cd168940d79b","source":"MONDO:0008954","target":"HP:0000239","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:214110 · OMIM:214110","url":"https://omim.org/entry/214110","level":"curated","date":"2009-02-17","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Peroxisome biogenesis disorder 2A (Zellweger): Large fontanelles [IEA]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.5,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.5},{"id":"MONDO:0013932","label":"peroxisome biogenesis disorder 5A (Zellweger)","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_2d4fc011b2c7","source":"MONDO:0013932","target":"HP:0000239","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":